{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they embittered their lives.</b> The speaking soul, which is the life of the body, in the manner of (Psalms 103:4): הגואל משחת חייכי — 'who redeems from the pit, your life.'" "<b>Also.</b> It is possible that the intent is upon the Holy One, blessed be He, for He is the life of the soul; and because of this Scripture did not say 'and they embittered their souls' (ואת נפשם). And one should not wonder at this, for explicitly the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: כי לי בני ישראל עבדים — 'the children of Israel are servants to Me'; whoever subjugates them from below is as if he subjugates them from above. And moreover, we find a full verse (Isaiah 63:9): בכל צרתם לא צר, and it is written (Psalms 91:15): עמו אנכי בצרה."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The citation from Psalms 103:4 in comment [0] is written with the rare long form חייכי (instead of the standard חייך); rendered as 'your life' accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:15.146826922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}